<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.5: Interpreting Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00951</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.5: Interpreting Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e866f0df-f6ac-4f0a-b8e5-6b0d06f10374</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">A squirrel runs up and down a tree.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">The graph shows the height of the squirrel, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (feet), as a function of time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (seconds).</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        
          <media alt="A line graph shows height in feet vs. time in seconds. Height rises to 14 feet at about 1.5 sec, drops to 0 at 4 sec, then quickly rises to 10 feet and levels off from 6 to 8 sec.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">What is the highest point the squirrel reaches?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00007">14 feet</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Solve <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What does this solution tell you about the squirrel?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> means that after 4 seconds, the squirrel is at the bottom of the tree on the ground.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">Find the vertical intercept of the graph. What does it tell you about the squirrel?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00015"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> means that at the beginning, the squirrel is 9 feet high in the tree.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>
